CORE gcc-only
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* pointer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* nested: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* evaluated once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* zero: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The GNU extension `a ?: b' (elfutils): the value of a if it is nonzero, with a
evaluated once, else that of b.  The C++ parser required an operand after `?'.
